	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "A Common Data Element (CDE) is a standardized, precisely defined question, paired with a set of allowable responses, used systematically across different sites, studies, or clinical trials to ensure consistent data collection. Multiple CDEs (from one or more Collections) can be curated into Forms. (https://cde.nlm.nih.gov/home)" ;
