	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "outcome" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An entity that has the role of being the consequence of an exposure event. This is an abstract mixin grouping of various categories of possible biological or non-biological (e.g. clinical) outcomes." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/biolink/biolink-model> .
<https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/PairwiseGeneToGeneInteraction> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> , <https://w3id.org/linkml/ClassDefinition> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "pairwise gene to gene interaction" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/biolink/vocab/GeneToGeneAssociation> , _:c14n1577 , _:c14n728 , _:c14n867 ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "An interaction between two genes or two gene products. May be physical (e.g. protein binding) or genetic (between genes). May be symmetric (e.g. protein interaction) or directed (e.g. phosphorylation)" ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://w3id.org/biolink/biolink-model> ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#narrowMatch> <https://datacommons.org/browser/ProteinProteinInteraction> .
