	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Holds between an intervention and a medical condition, and reports that a clinical trial  is being or has been performed in human patients to test the potential of the intervention to treat the medical condition (e.g. to ameliorate, stabilize, or cure the condition, or to delay, prevent, or reduce the risk of it manifesting in the first place)." ;
	<http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "This predicate should be used when a source reports a clinical trial where the intervention is being or was interrogated, regardless of the phase of the trial, or its ultimate outcome.  Information about phase and outcome can be capture using other modeling elements." ;
